  <event id="163">
      <start>10:15</start>
      <duration>00:30</duration>
      <room>AW1.125</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>VMKit</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Free Java</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The talk will describe &lt;a href=&#34;http://vmkit.llvm.org/&#34;&gt;VMKit&lt;/a&gt;, a Java virtual machine and CLI implementation (.Net is Microsoft&amp;#39;s implementation of the CLI) on top of the LLVM compiler infrastructure.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It will enlighten the benefits of using a shared compiler infrastructure such as LLVM as well as the current limitations. Finally, the talk will introduce VM experiments happening in the JVM implementation.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="1631">Nicolas Geoffray</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>